<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan's Parke-Davis falls 1.27 pct.</title>
<headline>Pakistan's Parke-Davis falls 1.27 pct.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Parke-Davis, a pharmaceuticals firm, fell five rupees, or 1.27 percent, to 390 in early trading on Tuesday after announcing what was seen as a disappointing final dividend, dealers said.</p>
<p>Parke-Davis announced a 90 percent final cash dividend for the financial year ended November 30, in addition to a 90 percent interim dividend already paid, one dealer said.</p>
<p>The firm paid a 160 percent dividend for the previous year.</p>
<p>About 100 of Parke-Davis's 10-rupee shares changed hands in early trade at the Karachi Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
